    <DataNode elementId="AT1G20020-MONOMER" textLabel="Ferredoxin--NADP reductase, leaf isozyme 2, chloroplastic" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q8W493" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="750" centerY="695" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">The leaf ferredoxin-NADP+-oxidoreductase (AtLFNR2) catalyzing the formation of NADPH from reduced ferredoxin and NADP has been characterized in &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. AtLFNR2 functions in close relationship with another ferredoxin-NADP+-oxidoreductase (AtLFNR1) which is necessary to attach it to the thylakoid membrane and with which it forms a functional heterodimer to regulate the distribution of electrons between the cyclic and linear electron transfer pathways |CITS: [17335513]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT1G20020-MONOMER" />
      <Property key="AlternativeId_Araport" value="AT1G20020.1" />
